  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-04T23:19:00.480Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Avatar ripping is a malicious act, arguably more harmful than in-game cheating. It severely discourages content creators, infringes upon the copyrights of the original artists, and damages the creative ecosystem of VRChat. Many talented creators have already been forced to stop creating or have even quit the platform entirely due to this issue. While new encryption methods can help, it's often only a matter of time before they are cracked.\n\nI propose the implementation of a Private Avatar Visibility Whitelist feature.\n\nThis system would allow users to specify a list of trusted friends. Only the users on this whitelist would be able to download and load the user's private avatar. For all other players not on the list, the system would only show the user's designated public/fallback avatar, and the private avatar's data would not be sent to their client at all. This feature should also be a toggleable option in the settings.\n\nThis approach would tackle a significant portion of the avatar ripping problem at its root. It would give creators who fear their work being stolen a powerful and reliable option to protect themselves and share their private avatars only with people they trust. At the same time, users who are willing to accept the risk can simply keep the feature turned off. This provides a necessary choice and empowers creators to control their own content.",
